# TEMPLATE: a floor's guardian: it holds the stairs and stands two knights
# tall (32 pixels). Its fight builds by stages of its health (the opening,
# the middle from 70%, its rage below `rage`), and from the middle on its
# charge-ups are its signature moments.
# Copy this file, then change what it says. Check it with
#   cargo run -p angel-delve --example content_check -- <your file>
#
# Change: as foe-chief.boss: name, text, by, where, hp, size, move, attacks,
#   phases (2 to 4 named patterns walked in turn), windups, rage, drops, art.
# Keep: the opening gentle (one attack, read one shot at a time), the middle
#   adding a second line, the rage the third or the phases; two windups, the
#   second `from=middle`; each stage inside its budget.
# The bar: art 24 to 32 rows tall (at most 32 by 32), drawn wide enough for its
#   size; graded Fine or better (a template, Masterwork).
name THE IRON WARDEN
text Stone and iron set to keep the stair: copy it and make it yours.
by angelX
where crypt
hp 820
size 1.8
move drift speed=1.0
attack ring shots=8 speed=5 every=115 damage=10 shot=bone
attack aimed shots=3 speed=7 every=77 damage=12 shot=bone from=middle
phases darts gap_wall every=140 volleys=2 damage=11 from=rage
windup slam every=220 damage=16 shots=2 speed=5 arc=60 cry=HNNNG
windup beam every=260 damage=14 arc=90 cry=hmmmm from=middle
rage 35%
drops gold 200, gem 2
